The Lorentz factor is

\[
\gamma=\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-v^2/c^2}}
=\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-(0.99999987)^2}}
\approx 1961.
\]

The Large Magellanic Cloud is approximately \(160{,}000\) light-years away. In Earth's frame, the journey takes about \(160{,}000\) years, but the astronaut experiences the proper time

\[
\tau=\frac{t}{\gamma}
\approx \frac{160{,}000}{1961}
\approx 81.6\text{ years}.
\]

Thus, the astronaut experiences approximately \(81\) years of travel and arrives at an age of roughly \(103\), within their 150-year lifespan.

