The salts dissociate to provide the conjugate acid–base pair \(\mathrm{H_2PO_4^-}/\mathrm{HPO_4^{2-}}\).

\[
[\mathrm{H_2PO_4^-}]_0
=\frac{1.00/136.09}{0.20000}
=0.03674\ \mathrm{M}
\]

\[
[\mathrm{HPO_4^{2-}}]_0
=\frac{1.00/177.99}{0.20000}
=0.02809\ \mathrm{M}
\]

Using \(K_{a2}\):

\[
[\mathrm{H^+}]
=K_{a2}\frac{[\mathrm{H_2PO_4^-}]}{[\mathrm{HPO_4^{2-}}]}
=(6.2\times10^{-8})\frac{0.03674}{0.02809}
=8.11\times10^{-8}\ \mathrm{M}
\]

For the third dissociation,

\[
K_{a3}=\frac{[\mathrm{H^+}][\mathrm{PO_4^{3-}}]}
{[\mathrm{HPO_4^{2-}}]}
\]

so

\[
[\mathrm{PO_4^{3-}}]
=\frac{K_{a3}[\mathrm{HPO_4^{2-}}]}{[\mathrm{H^+}]}
=\frac{(1.8\times10^{-12})(0.02809)}
{8.11\times10^{-8}}
=6.24\times10^{-7}\ \mathrm{M}
\]

